Copyright (c) 2026 Mayonesu0 (https://github.com/Mayonesu0). All rights reserved,
except the permissions written below.

"Chop!" means the mod of that name: its source code, its files, its texts and images,
and every version of them, published at https://github.com/Mayonesu0/chop or through
Horizon's mod registry.

The source code of Chop! is public so that players and Horizon's reviewers can see what
it does. That does not make it free software: you may read it, but you may not copy it,
change it or reuse it except as written here.

1. Players

   You may download Chop! from Horizon's mod registry, from the Horizon launcher or from
   the repository above, and use it unchanged:
   - have the Horizon launcher (or `horizon-launcher native-build`) compile it into
     Horizon, the way the launcher builds every native mod;
   - play with it in single player, on LAN and on servers you host or run;
   - share screenshots and videos of it, and talk about it.

2. Horizon's registry

   The Horizon project and the maintainers of its mod registry
   (https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon-mods) may store, mirror and distribute
   unchanged copies of the files of Chop! that Mayonesu0 submits, list them in the
   registry's index, show them on its pages and in the launcher, and keep them
   available, or take them down, as the registry's rules say.

3. Horizon's reviewers

   Horizon's reviewers and maintainers may read the whole source of Chop!, build it,
   run it and test it to review it, and quote parts of it in their review. This is the
   written grant asked for by Horizon's mod policy ("Licences reviewers can read").

4. What is not allowed

   Without Mayonesu0's prior written permission, you may not:
   - copy the source code of Chop!, in whole or in part, into another project;
   - modify Chop!, or distribute or publish a modified version of it, or a work derived
     from it;
   - distribute Chop! anywhere else than through the registry and the repository above,
     or sell it;
   - publish another mod under the name "Chop!" or present your work as Chop!;
   - remove or change this licence or the copyright notice.

   Forking the repository on GitHub, as GitHub's Terms of Service allow, gives you no
   other right than the ones above.

5. No warranty

   Chop! is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied. In no
   event shall Mayonesu0 be liable for any claim, damages or other liability arising
   from Chop! or from its use.

6. End of the permissions

   Anyone who breaks this licence loses the permissions it gives them.

To ask for a permission, open an issue on https://github.com/Mayonesu0/chop.

Chop! is not an official Minecraft product, and is not approved by or associated with
Mojang or Microsoft. Horizon is a separate project, under its own licence.

